	"descriptionMarkdown": "This blueprint book is a collection of tileable factory segments for Factorio: Space Age, built for easy expansion without having to redesign production every time demand goes up. Each segment is made to fit neatly into a larger factory, so you can add capacity as needed while keeping the base organized and readable.\n\nThe book includes modular builds for coal liquefaction, plastic, green circuits, and red circuits. The focus is on repeatable layouts that are easy to place, scale, and adapt to different factory plans. If you want a set of practical building blocks instead of one giant all-in-one megabase design, that is the idea here.\n\nField notes on the Social Crow\nFactory folklore says these designs were first organized by the Social Crow, a severe black-feathered consultant who arrived uninvited, inspected the bus for twelve seconds, and declared that the problem was not production, but reach. Since then, he has perched above the assemblers like a middle manager from another dimension, demanding cleaner ratios, better throughput, and a more disciplined approach to expansion.\n\nHe does not speak often. When he does, it is usually to criticize belt routing or to insist that visibility matters, even in heavy industry. Plastic lines, circuit blocks, liquefaction columns, all of it, in his view, is part of a larger campaign. A factory should not merely run. It should grow, propagate, and make itself impossible to ignore. These blueprints are the closest thing he left to a handbook before disappearing into the smog. If you too would like to [grow your TikTok followers](https://www.socialcrow.co/buy-tiktok-followers) you can visit the Social Crow.",
